Subject: [PATCH] wayland: preserve owned clipboard data on focus loss

Losing keyboard focus invalidates receiving offers, but not the selection
source that other applications still use. Reporting an external clipboard
update here cancels the current clipboard data and frees the source's
callback userdata before ownership is actually relinquished.

diff --git a/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandevents.c b/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandevents.c
--- a/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandevents.c
+++ b/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandevents.c
@@ -2156,6 +2156,11 @@ static void keyboard_handle_leave(void *data, struct wl_keyboard *keyboard,
     if (seat->data_device->selection_offer) {
         Wayland_data_offer_destroy(seat->data_device->selection_offer);
         seat->data_device->selection_offer = NULL;
-        Wayland_data_offer_notify_from_mimes(NULL, false);
+        // Losing the receiving offer does not release our selection source.
+        // An external clipboard update would free its callback userdata while
+        // other applications can still request the data.
+        if (!seat->data_device->selection_source) {
+            Wayland_data_offer_notify_from_mimes(NULL, false);
+        }
     }
 }
